# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# In Search of Dharma — public repository ignore rules
# Anything listed here is intentionally kept OUT of the public repo:
# internal instructions, private author/method material, and local cruft.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Internal / AI-assistant instructions — never published
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Part 0 research: all seven notes are published as redacted public editions;
# only the private substrate is withheld — the mail archive, the seed
# correspondence, and the unredacted originals.
# The finished, public-facing preface is 0-preface.md at the repo root.
0-preface/.mail/
0-preface/.llms/
0-preface/.private/
0-preface/_seed.md

# Deployment targets: machine names and server paths, kept out of the public
# repository. deploy.conf.example is tracked and shows the required keys.
deploy.conf

# Internal working documents — filed under wip/ (entire tree ignored).
# The root-level patterns below remain as safety nets for working files
# that habitually land at the root before being filed into wip/.
wip/
copy-to-workshops.sh
rupert-reply.md
ramsey-*.md
critical-review*.md
critique-*.md
CRITIQUE.md
TODO.md

# Prose-hygiene sub-project: harvested source material (transcripts, comment
# threads, style teardowns) used to identify and strip AI-generated tics,
# structures and word choices from the manuscript. Third-party content and
# working notes — kept local, never published.
docs/ai-writing/

# Assets not yet cleared for publication
# (no trailing slash: www is a symlink, and dir-only patterns skip symlinks)
www

# Local tooling / environment / OS cruft
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
scratch/
.DS_Store

# superpowers SDD scratch (ledger, briefs, reports)
.superpowers/

# generated Hugging Face dataset export (mk-hf-dataset.py output)
hf-dataset/

# page-render previews of the built book (spot-check byproduct, regenerable)
pg-*.png
9-defining-dharma_watercolor.v*

# audio-embedded EPUB (~70 MB of bundled MP3s). The `--audio embed` build was
# retired from mk-book.sh in 1.2.0; the pattern stays so a copy left over from
# an earlier build can never be committed by accident.
*_with-audio.epub

# typeface proofs (`./mk-book.sh --fonts SET` for any set but the default).
# Built to be looked at and printed while a typeface decision is open, then
# thrown away; only the shipping edition's EPUB and PDF stay tracked. Suffixes
# match FONT_SETS in lib/fonts.sh.
*_classic.epub
*_classic.pdf
*_worksans.epub
*_worksans.pdf
*_bonanova.epub
*_bonanova.pdf
*_bonanova-solo.epub
*_bonanova-solo.pdf

# Printer's reference material from Tuwhiri: their book extract, IngramSpark's
# file checklist, and Ramsey's marked-up typographic specs. Third-party
# copyright, supplied for reference only. This repository is public, so none of
# it may ever be committed. The measurements taken from these files live in
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-print-interior-pdf-design.md, which is the
# durable record; the files themselves are disposable.
print/

# The print interior, rebuilt on demand from the sources like every other
# artefact in this list.
In-Search-of-Dharma_interior_*.pdf

# Ramsey's working document for the cover copy; the author's final version
# lives in print-cover-text.md.
cover-text-In-search-of-dharma.rtf
cover text In search of dharma.*
# Derived from print-cover-text.md for correspondents who cannot open Markdown.
print-cover-text.docx

# Correspondence tools: the mailbox they read is one person's, so its
# location and the record of what has been seen stay local.
tools/mail.conf
tools/.mailwatch.seen
